␛[1;4mvocab_unknown␛[0m

A value is not in the vocabulary its field uses.

Severity: error. Reported by ␛[1;36mopentide validate␛[0m (schema check).

␛[1mExample␛[0m

␛[36m    metadata:␛[0m
␛[36m      tlp: clearr          # tlp::1.0 has clear, green, amber, amber+strict, red␛[0m

␛[1mHow to fix␛[0m

Use a value from the vocabulary the label names. When a close value exists, ␛[1;36mhelp␛[0m names it and ␛[1;36mfix␛[0m
carries the edit; the edit is marked ␛[1;36msafe␛[0m only when the two spell the same word (they differ in
case, spaces, ␛[1;36m-␛[0m or ␛[1;36m_␛[0m) and hold no digit, so an ATT&CK id is never replaced unreviewed. The opentide
VS Code extension completes vocabulary values (␛[1;36mopentide setup vscode␛[0m recommends it).

